# Hardened sshd config for the homie demo output-card sandbox. This is the
# ONLY thing a public demo visitor can reach via SSH - see README.md in this
# directory for the full threat model. Every restriction here is deliberate;
# don't loosen any of it without re-reading that README first.

Port 2222
ListenAddress 0.0.0.0

# Key-only, one user, no root, no interactive shell of any kind - the
# per-key `command=` forced-command in authorized_keys is what actually runs
# (see allowed-command.sh), never a real shell.
PermitRootLogin no
PasswordAuthentication no
KbdInteractiveAuthentication no
PubkeyAuthentication yes
AllowUsers sandbox
MaxAuthTries 3
MaxSessions 4
LoginGraceTime 10

# No forwarding, no tunneling, no agent, no PTY - belt and suspenders on top
# of the same restrictions already set per-key in authorized_keys.
AllowTcpForwarding no
AllowStreamLocalForwarding no
GatewayPorts no
PermitTunnel no
X11Forwarding no
AllowAgentForwarding no
PermitTTY no
PrintMotd no

# UsePAM/PrintLastLog omitted deliberately - this Alpine sshd build has no
# PAM support compiled in and rejects both as unsupported directives (a
# startup warning, not fatal, but worth not carrying dead config).
StrictModes yes
Subsystem sftp /bin/false
